${macro.generated_by(self.path)}

=[ Catasto ]

Filesystem schema, manifest, and lockfile toolchain (`fs-catasto`).

==[ Overview ]

`catasto` defines and verifies filesystem schemas, directory rules, naming conventions, media manifests, and content lockfiles (SHA-256 and provenance) across a workspace.

Just as a cadastre (*catasto*) records the boundaries, parcels, and ownership of land, `catasto` keeps a repository's directory tree reproducible and governed by explicit rules.

==[ Usage ]

```bash
catasto sync [path]    # fetch every managed file from its source, then lock
catasto lock [path]    # record the sha256 of every managed file in catasto.lock
catasto check [path]   # report drift between catasto.toml, catasto.lock, and the files
```

`check` exits with 1 when it finds drift. Files that are neither declared nor locked are unmanaged and never reported.

==[ Files ]

`catasto.toml` is written by hand and declares the managed files and where each one comes from.

```toml
[[managed]]
path = "tmtroot/schema/vocabularies/writ.vocabulary.tmt"
source = { path = "../vocabularies/writ.vocabulary.tmt" }
```

`path` is relative to the workspace and must stay inside it. `source` is relative to the workspace root and may point outside it. Only local paths are supported so far.

`catasto.lock` is generated by `catasto lock` and `catasto sync`. Commit it together with the managed files, so a fresh clone can run `catasto check` without the sources.

==[ Drift ]

-| `modified` -- the file differs from its locked sha256.
-| `missing` -- the file does not exist.
-| `stale` -- the source differs from the locked sha256. Reported only when the source is readable.
-| `unlocked` -- declared, but the lock has no entry or records another source.
-| `orphaned` -- locked, but no longer declared.

==[ Workspace Layout ]

-| @dir(app) (`catasto-cli`) -- Main CLI binary (`catasto`). Layer 1.
-| @dir(crates/catasto-core) (`catasto-core`) -- Core library for filesystem schema parsing, directory rule evaluation, and lockfile verification. Layer 0.

==[ Building and Testing ]

=== Build workspace
```bash
cargo build --workspace
```

=== Run tests
```bash
cargo test --workspace
```

=== Check workspace
```bash
cargo run -p catasto-cli -- check .
```
